Witness of linux-packing-le-oob (lib/packing.c, calculate_box_addr(), via
pack() / unpack()).

  make LINUX=<kernel tree> run   non-zero exit while the bug is there

Self-contained: compiles the tree's lib/packing.c with compat.h (copied
from hegel-c's tests/irl/linux/packing_roundtrip/), ASan and UBSan on.

Expected at v7.1 (8cd9520d35a6), checked 2026-11-07:
  SUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow .../lib/packing.c:155 in __pack
  exit 1

With hegel-c's fix (tests/irl/linux/pins/packing_roundtrip.patch, the
pin's fixed state), checked 2026-11-07:
  pack(1-byte buffer, bit 0, QUIRK_LITTLE_ENDIAN) stayed in bounds
  exit 0

The repro is the write-up's own minimal case.  hegel-c's pin
tests/irl/linux/pins/packing_roundtrip.conf runs the round-trip property
(unpack (pack (x)) == x) that found the bug, red then green the same way.
